{"title":"Career Roadmap · Quality Control Analyst","role":"Quality Control Analyst","summary":"A Quality Control (QC) Analyst tests raw materials, in-process samples, finished products, and environmental samples to determine whether they meet defined quality, safety, purity, identity, and performance specifications.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Chemistry"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Quality Control (QC) Analyst tests raw materials, in-process samples, finished products, and environmental samples to determine whether they meet defined quality, safety, purity, identity, and performance specifications."},{"type":"p","text":"For a Chemistry graduate, this is one of the most direct career pathways because the role depends heavily on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Analytical chemistry"},{"text":"Organic/inorganic chemistry"},{"text":"Instrumentation"},{"text":"Laboratory techniques"},{"text":"Quantitative analysis"},{"text":"Sample preparation"},{"text":"Method validation"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Data interpretation"},{"text":"Laboratory safety"}]},{"type":"p","text":"QC Analysts are employed across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Biotechnology"},{"text":"Chemicals"},{"text":"Food and beverages"},{"text":"Cosmetics"},{"text":"Petrochemicals"},{"text":"Environmental laboratories"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Water testing"},{"text":"Medical products"},{"text":"Specialty chemicals"},{"text":"Manufacturing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Chemistry","Analytical Instrumentation","GMP/GLP","Documentation","Data Integrity","Statistical Quality Control"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc. Chemistry"},{"text":"Analytical chemistry + laboratory skills"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"QC Analyst / Laboratory Analyst"},{"text":"Routine testing + instrumentation"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior QC Analyst / QC Specialist"},{"text":"Method validation + investigations"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"QC Lead / Laboratory Manager / Quality Specialist"},{"text":"Quality systems + laboratory leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"Build the Chemistry Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"During B.Sc., develop strong theoretical and practical knowledge."},{"type":"h","text":"Core chemistry"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Organic chemistry"},{"text":"Inorganic chemistry"},{"text":"Physical chemistry"},{"text":"Analytical chemistry"},{"text":"Biochemistry fundamentals"},{"text":"Electrochemistry"},{"text":"Spectroscopy"},{"text":"Chemical kinetics"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Particularly important for QC"},{"type":"p","text":"Analytical Chemistry should become the strongest subject."},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Qualitative analysis"},{"text":"Quantitative analysis"},{"text":"Volumetric analysis"},{"text":"Gravimetric analysis"},{"text":"Titration"},{"text":"Separation techniques"},{"text":"Chromatography"},{"text":"Spectroscopy"},{"text":"Electroanalytical methods"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Laboratory Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop disciplined laboratory habits."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Laboratory safety"},{"text":"Chemical handling"},{"text":"PPE"},{"text":"Solution preparation"},{"text":"Dilution"},{"text":"Concentration calculations"},{"text":"Molarity"},{"text":"Normality"},{"text":"Standardization"},{"text":"pH measurement"},{"text":"Titration"},{"text":"Weighing"},{"text":"Pipetting"},{"text":"Filtration"},{"text":"Sample preparation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Fundamental workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sample","Identification","Sample Preparation","Measurement","Calculation","Result","Specification Comparison","Pass / Fail"]},{"type":"p","text":"The important professional habit is traceability: another trained person should be able to understand how the result was generated."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Analytical Chemistry"},{"type":"p","text":"This becomes the technical core of the career."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn quantitative techniques"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Acid-base titration"},{"text":"Redox titration"},{"text":"Complexometric titration"},{"text":"Precipitation titration"},{"text":"Gravimetric analysis"},{"text":"Potentiometry"},{"text":"Conductometry"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Separation techniques"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Filtration"},{"text":"Extraction"},{"text":"Distillation"},{"text":"Crystallization"},{"text":"Chromatography"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then progress to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"TLC"},{"text":"HPLC"},{"text":"GC"},{"text":"Ion chromatography"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2–3 — Analytical Instrumentation"},{"type":"p","text":"A modern QC Analyst must become comfortable with laboratory instruments."},{"type":"h","text":"UV-Visible Spectroscopy"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Beer-Lambert law"},{"text":"Absorbance"},{"text":"Transmittance"},{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Standard curves"},{"text":"Quantification"}]},{"type":"h","text":"FTIR"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Molecular vibrations"},{"text":"Functional-group identification"},{"text":"Spectral interpretation"},{"text":"Reference spectrum comparison"}]},{"type":"h","text":"HPLC"},{"type":"p","text":"One of the most valuable skills for pharmaceutical and chemical QC."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mobile phase"},{"text":"Stationary phase"},{"text":"Columns"},{"text":"Injection"},{"text":"Retention time"},{"text":"Peak area"},{"text":"Peak height"},{"text":"Resolution"},{"text":"System suitability"},{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Quantification"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sample","Preparation","Filtration","HPLC Injection","Chromatogram","Peak Identification","Peak Integration","Calculation","Specification Comparison","Report"]},{"type":"h","text":"GC"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gas chromatography fundamentals"},{"text":"Carrier gases"},{"text":"Columns"},{"text":"Injection"},{"text":"Retention time"},{"text":"Detector concepts"},{"text":"Chromatogram interpretation"},{"text":"Quantification"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Volatile compounds"},{"text":"Solvents"},{"text":"Residual solvents"},{"text":"Petrochemical analysis"},{"text":"Chemical products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Pharmaceutical & Industrial QC"},{"type":"p","text":"If targeting pharma or regulated manufacturing, understand the overall quality environment."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn concepts such as"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GMP"},{"text":"GLP"},{"text":"SOPs"},{"text":"Specifications"},{"text":"Batch records"},{"text":"Laboratory records"},{"text":"Sample management"},{"text":"Stability testing"},{"text":"OOS"},{"text":"OOT"},{"text":"CAPA"},{"text":"Change control"},{"text":"Deviations"},{"text":"Data integrity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important distinction"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QC primarily tests and evaluates materials/products."},{"text":"QA focuses more broadly on systems, processes, compliance, and quality assurance."},{"text":"A QC Analyst should understand both, but build deep expertise in laboratory testing first."}]},{"type":"h","text":"OOS Investigation"},{"type":"p","text":"One of the most important professional skills is understanding Out-of-Specification (OOS) results."},{"type":"p","text":"A simplified workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Unexpected Result","Check Calculation","Review Instrument Status","Check Sample Preparation","Review Method","Check Raw Data","Document Findings","Laboratory Investigation","Root-Cause Evaluation","Corrective / Preventive Action"]},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"An analyst should never simply repeat a test until a passing result appears."},{"text":"The investigation must follow the applicable laboratory procedure and quality system."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3–4 — Method Validation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop foundational knowledge of analytical method validation."},{"type":"p","text":"Important parameters include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accuracy"},{"text":"Precision"},{"text":"Specificity"},{"text":"Linearity"},{"text":"Range"},{"text":"Detection limit"},{"text":"Quantitation limit"},{"text":"Robustness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"flow","items":["Analytical Method","Specificity","Accuracy","Precision","Linearity","Range","Detection / Quantitation Limits","Robustness","Validated Method"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact validation expectations depend on the industry, product, method, and applicable regulatory framework."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3–4 — Quality Control Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"QC is not just chemistry; it is also measurement science and statistics."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Relative standard deviation"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Control charts"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Trend analysis"},{"text":"Measurement uncertainty"},{"text":"Calibration curves"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Statistical process control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important calculations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Standard Deviation"},{"text":"%RSD"},{"text":"Recovery %"},{"text":"Assay %"},{"text":"Purity %"},{"text":"Concentration"},{"text":"Dilution Factor"},{"text":"Calibration Curve"},{"text":"Correlation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data Integrity & Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"This is critical in regulated laboratories."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accurate recording"},{"text":"Traceability"},{"text":"Original data"},{"text":"Controlled documentation"},{"text":"Audit trails"},{"text":"Electronic records"},{"text":"Instrument records"},{"text":"Sample traceability"},{"text":"Review and approval"},{"text":"For regulated environments, understand the concept of ALCOA+ data integrity principles and how they apply to laboratory records."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Laboratory Software & Digital Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"A modern QC Analyst should not be limited to manual laboratory work."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Laboratory Information Management Systems (LIMS)"},{"text":"Electronic laboratory systems"},{"text":"Instrument data systems"},{"text":"Basic statistical software"},{"text":"Basic Python or R"},{"text":"Data visualization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Excel"},{"type":"p","text":"Become comfortable with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Formulas"},{"text":"Pivot tables"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Data validation"},{"text":"Statistical calculations"},{"text":"Trend analysis"},{"text":"Automated reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"LIMS"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the role of a Laboratory Information Management System."},{"type":"flow","items":["Sample Received","Sample Registration","Test Assignment","Analyst","Instrument Result","Data Review","Specification Check","Approval","QC Report"]},{"type":"p","text":"LIMS knowledge can be a strong differentiator when applying to modern laboratories."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Laboratory Quality Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Build understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SOP management"},{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Instrument qualification"},{"text":"Preventive maintenance"},{"text":"Reference standards"},{"text":"Reagents"},{"text":"Retention samples"},{"text":"Stability programs"},{"text":"Internal audits"},{"text":"External audits"},{"text":"Deviations"},{"text":"CAPA"},{"text":"Change control"},{"text":"Risk management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Major Instrumentation Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Instrument / Technique","Target Level"],"rows":[[{"text":"Analytical Balance"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"pH Meter"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"UV-Vis"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"FTIR"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Conductometer"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"Potentiometer"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"HPLC"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"GC"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"TLC"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Dissolution Testing"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"Karl Fischer"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"AAS"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"ICP-OES"},{"text":"Basic–Intermediate"}],[{"text":"LC-MS"},{"text":"Basic"}],[{"text":"GC-MS"},{"text":"Basic"}],[{"text":"NMR"},{"text":"Basic"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"You do not need expert-level knowledge of every instrument. The ideal depth depends on the industry and target employer."},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project Ideas"}]},{"heading":"HPLC Method Development / Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Work on quantitative analysis using HPLC where appropriate."},{"type":"p","text":"Demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sample preparation"},{"text":"Standard preparation"},{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Chromatogram interpretation"},{"text":"Precision"},{"text":"Accuracy"},{"text":"Data reporting"}]}]},{"heading":"UV-Visible Quantitative Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop a calibration curve and determine concentration of a suitable analyte."},{"type":"p","text":"Show:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Standard preparation"},{"text":"Absorbance measurements"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Accuracy"},{"text":"Precision"},{"text":"Results"}]}]},{"heading":"Pharmaceutical Quality Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study quality parameters for a suitable pharmaceutical product using appropriate analytical techniques."}]},{"heading":"Water Quality Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Analyse parameters such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pH"},{"text":"Conductivity"},{"text":"Hardness"},{"text":"Chloride"},{"text":"Dissolved solids"},{"text":"Selected chemical contaminants"}]}]},{"heading":"QC Statistical Dashboard","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Create an Excel/Power BI dashboard for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Batch results"},{"text":"Assay trends"},{"text":"OOS events"},{"text":"Instrument performance"},{"text":"Analyst performance"},{"text":"Stability trends"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["This project combines Chemistry","QC","Data Analytics."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"Start laboratory internships as early as practical."},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QC Intern"},{"text":"Quality Control Laboratory Intern"},{"text":"Analytical Chemistry Intern"},{"text":"Pharmaceutical Analysis Intern"},{"text":"Stability Testing Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Chemical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Chemical QC Intern"},{"text":"Analytical Laboratory Intern"},{"text":"Process QC Intern"},{"text":"Chemical Testing Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Food"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Food Quality Intern"},{"text":"Food Testing Laboratory Intern"},{"text":"Analytical Testing Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Environmental"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Environmental Laboratory Intern"},{"text":"Water Quality Testing Intern"},{"text":"Environmental Chemistry Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Analytical Chemistry Research Intern"},{"text":"Laboratory Research Intern"},{"text":"Instrumentation Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Entry-Level Career Options"},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant roles include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality Control Analyst"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QC Chemist"},{"text":"Junior QC Analyst"},{"text":"QC Executive"},{"text":"Analytical Chemist"},{"text":"Laboratory Analyst"},{"text":"Quality Control Chemist"},{"text":"Analytical Testing Associate"},{"text":"Laboratory Executive"},{"text":"Quality Testing Analyst"},{"text":"Chemical Analyst"},{"text":"Stability Analyst"},{"text":"Instrumentation Analyst"},{"text":"Microbiology QC Associate — requires relevant microbiology training"},{"text":"Raw Material Analyst"},{"text":"Finished Product Analyst"},{"text":"Environmental Laboratory Analyst"},{"text":"Research Laboratory Analyst"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Industry","High-Value Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Pharmaceuticals"},{"text":"HPLC + GMP + Documentation"}],[{"text":"Biotechnology"},{"text":"Analytical testing + GMP"}],[{"text":"Chemicals"},{"text":"Analytical chemistry + GC/HPLC"}],[{"text":"Food"},{"text":"Food chemistry + QC"}],[{"text":"Cosmetics"},{"text":"Analytical testing + formulation knowledge"}],[{"text":"Petrochemicals"},{"text":"GC + analytical chemistry"}],[{"text":"Environmental"},{"text":"Water/soil/chemical analysis"}],[{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Instrumental analysis"}],[{"text":"Contract Testing"},{"text":"Multi-instrument capability"}],[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Instrumentation + scientific analysis"}],[{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"QC + process understanding"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Certifications & Learning"},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize practical laboratory competence."},{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Analytical Chemistry"},{"text":"HPLC"},{"text":"GC"},{"text":"Spectroscopy"},{"text":"GMP"},{"text":"GLP"},{"text":"Method Validation"},{"text":"Data Integrity"},{"text":"LIMS"},{"text":"Statistical Quality Control"},{"text":"Laboratory Safety"},{"text":"For regulated-industry certifications, verify current recognition and employer relevance before paying for a course."}]},{"type":"h","text":"PG Options"},{"type":"h","text":"Chemistry"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc. Analytical Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc. Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc. Industrial Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc. Pharmaceutical Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc. Organic Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc. Inorganic Chemistry"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strongest choice for QC"},{"type":"h","text":"M.Sc. Analytical Chemistry"},{"type":"p","text":"because it deepens:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Instrumentation"},{"text":"Chromatography"},{"text":"Spectroscopy"},{"text":"Method development"},{"text":"Quantitative analysis"},{"text":"Quality testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Relevant PG Paths"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc. Industrial Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc. Pharmaceutical Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc. Quality Management"},{"text":"Pharmaceutical Sciences programs, where eligible"},{"text":"Regulatory Affairs"},{"text":"Biotechnology, depending on eligibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Pharmaceutical QC"},{"type":"flow","items":["Chemistry","HPLC","GMP","Method Validation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"One of the strongest routes."},{"type":"h","text":"2. Analytical Chemistry"},{"type":"flow","items":["Instrumentation","Method Development","Validation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Suitable for laboratories and analytical service organizations."},{"type":"h","text":"3. Chemical Industry QC"},{"type":"flow","items":["Chemistry","GC/HPLC","Process Quality"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"4. Stability Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stability protocols"},{"text":"Degradation"},{"text":"Analytical testing"},{"text":"Trend analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Instrumentation Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Become highly skilled in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HPLC"},{"text":"GC"},{"text":"UV-Vis"},{"text":"FTIR"},{"text":"Other analytical instruments"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Quality Data Analyst"},{"type":"p","text":"An emerging hybrid path:"},{"type":"flow","items":["QC","Statistics","Excel/Power BI","LIMS","Data Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This can lead toward laboratory digitalization and quality analytics."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Progression"},{"type":"h","text":"Route 1 — Pharmaceutical QC"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc. Chemistry","QC Intern","QC Analyst / QC Chemist","Senior QC Analyst","QC Specialist","QC Supervisor","QC Manager","Quality Control Head"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route 2 — Analytical Chemistry"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc. Chemistry","Analytical Laboratory Intern","Analytical Chemist","Senior Analytical Chemist","Method Development Specialist","Analytical Science Lead","Laboratory / Technical Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route 3 — QC + Data"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc. Chemistry","QC Analyst","QC Data Analyst","Quality Analytics Specialist","Laboratory Data / Digital Quality Lead","Quality Systems / Analytics Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Laboratory Automation"},{"type":"p","text":"Automation is increasingly being used for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sample preparation"},{"text":"Liquid handling"},{"text":"High-throughput testing"},{"text":"Instrument integration"},{"text":"Data capture"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. AI-Assisted Analytical Chemistry"},{"type":"p","text":"AI can support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Chromatogram analysis"},{"text":"Spectral interpretation"},{"text":"Anomaly detection"},{"text":"Method optimization"},{"text":"Predictive quality analysis"},{"text":"But laboratory decisions still require appropriate scientific and quality-system oversight."}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Laboratory Digitalization"},{"type":"p","text":"The modern laboratory is moving toward:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Instrument","Electronic Data","LIMS","Automated Data Capture","Analytics","Quality Dashboard","Decision"]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Predictive Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"Historical QC data can be used to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Process drift"},{"text":"Recurring deviations"},{"text":"Instrument problems"},{"text":"Batch trends"},{"text":"Stability patterns"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. PAT & Real-Time Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"Process Analytical Technology can connect manufacturing processes with real-time measurement and process understanding."},{"type":"p","text":"This creates a bridge between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["QC","Process Engineering","Data Analytics","Automation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QC ANALYST"},{"text":"│"},{"text":"┌───────────────┼────────────────┐"},{"text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"text":"CHEMISTRY INSTRUMENTATION QUALITY"},{"text":"│ │ │"},{"text":"Analytical HPLC GMP"},{"text":"Organic GC GLP"},{"text":"Physical UV-Vis SOPs"},{"text":"Inorganic FTIR OOS"},{"text":"│ Chromatography CAPA"},{"text":"│ Spectroscopy Data Integrity"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["└───────────────┼────────────────┘","DATA SKILLS","Excel + Statistics","LIMS / Digital QC","Quality Analytics"]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong B.Sc. Chemistry graduate targeting QC should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Perform laboratory sample preparation"},{"text":"Prepare standards and solutions"},{"text":"Perform quantitative analysis"},{"text":"Conduct titrations"},{"text":"Operate basic analytical instruments"},{"text":"Understand UV-Vis and FTIR"},{"text":"Understand HPLC"},{"text":"Understand GC"},{"text":"Interpret chromatograms"},{"text":"Perform basic method validation"},{"text":"Calculate assay and purity"},{"text":"Apply QC statistics"},{"text":"Understand GMP/GLP"},{"text":"Follow SOPs"},{"text":"Maintain laboratory records"},{"text":"Understand data integrity"},{"text":"Use Excel for QC analysis"},{"text":"Understand LIMS workflows"},{"text":"Investigate laboratory anomalies systematically"},{"text":"Prepare technical reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"A Chemistry student should build a portfolio around laboratory evidence, not just theoretical projects."},{"type":"p","text":"Recommended:"},{"type":"h","text":"HPLC Analytical Study"},{"type":"h","text":"UV-Vis Quantitative Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Water Quality Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical/Industrial QC Study"},{"type":"h","text":"Analytical Method Validation Project"},{"type":"h","text":"QC Statistical Dashboard"},{"type":"h","text":"OOS Investigation Case Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Where possible, include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Experimental objective"},{"text":"Method"},{"text":"Sample preparation"},{"text":"Raw observations/data"},{"text":"Calculations"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Results"},{"text":"Specification comparison"},{"text":"Interpretation"},{"text":"Limitations"},{"text":"Conclusion"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"p","text":"“An analytical chemistry professional with strong laboratory, instrumental analysis, quality-system, statistical and documentation skills, capable of performing reliable testing and interpreting QC data in regulated manufacturing and laboratory environments.”"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc. Chemistry","Analytical Chemistry","Laboratory Skills","HPLC + GC + Spectroscopy","GMP + GLP + Data Integrity","Method Validation","QC Internship","QC Analyst / QC Chemist","Senior QC Analyst","QC Specialist","QC Supervisor / Manager","Quality Control / Laboratory Leadership"]},{"type":"note","label":"Best long-term combination","text":"B.Sc. Chemistry + Analytical Chemistry + HPLC/GC + Spectroscopy + GMP/GLP + Method Validation + QC Statistics + LIMS + Data Integrity + Quality Analytics."}]}]}